From: Ashwani <thesingletonclass@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: ploam: reset AES key_idx in ploam_reset()

ploam_reset() clears state, onu_id, omci_gem_configured, eqd, and pending key
exchange state on session teardown, but leaves pp->key_idx at its previous
session value. Reset pp->key_idx = 0 so every fresh activation begins AES key
exchange consistently from key index 0.

Signed-off-by: Ashwani <thesingletonclass@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.c
@@ -666,6 +666,7 @@
 {
 	pp->state                = GPON_O1_INITIAL;
 	pp->onu_id               = PLOAM_ONU_UNASSIGNED;
+	pp->key_idx              = 0;
 	pp->omci_gem_configured  = false;
 	pp->omci_gem_port        = 0;
 	pp->key_exchange_pending = false;
